WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.568 --> 00:00:04.737
-On Monday night, my next guests
became Stanley Cup champions.

00:00:04.737 --> 00:00:08.908
From the 2020 Stanley Cup
champion Tampa Bay Lightning,

00:00:08.908 --> 00:00:11.711
here are team captain
Steven Stamkos,

00:00:11.711 --> 00:00:16.249
Nikita Kucherov,
and MVP Victor Hedman!

00:00:16.249 --> 00:00:20.419
Congratulations, guys,
on winning the Stanley Cup.

00:00:20.419 --> 00:00:23.089
Steven, how did you guys
celebrate on Monday night?

00:00:23.089 --> 00:00:25.191
You don't have to
go into full detail.

00:00:25.191 --> 00:00:28.394
-Yeah, I don't know.
You name it, we did it.

00:00:28.394 --> 00:00:31.964
We -- This is the greatest
trophy in all of sports,

00:00:31.964 --> 00:00:34.367
but You can make whatever
the heck you want out of it.

00:00:34.367 --> 00:00:36.469
-[ Laughs ]
-There it is right there.

00:00:36.469 --> 00:00:38.571
We were drinking everything
out of there.

00:00:38.571 --> 00:00:40.973
You see the boys are drinking
in the background still.

00:00:40.973 --> 00:00:43.343
-Oh, my God.
They're troublemakers.

00:00:43.343 --> 00:00:44.877
Oh -- [ Laughs ]

00:00:44.877 --> 00:00:46.245
Now, obviously you guys --

00:00:46.245 --> 00:00:49.081
It's a tough sport.
Players get hit in hockey.

00:00:49.081 --> 00:00:51.885
Nikita, you got hit more times
than usual

00:00:51.885 --> 00:00:53.953
in just one game against Dallas.

00:00:53.953 --> 00:00:56.155
We have video of this.
Take a look at this.

00:00:56.155 --> 00:00:57.457
-...runs into Jamie Benn.

00:00:57.457 --> 00:01:00.359
-Bop! Right there.
That was enough for me.

00:01:00.359 --> 00:01:01.861
And then -- Oosh!

00:01:01.861 --> 00:01:03.830
That's when I started crying.

00:01:03.830 --> 00:01:08.167
And here's -- Bang!
Right in the head.

00:01:08.167 --> 00:01:12.005
Now, do you know
where you are right now?

00:01:12.005 --> 00:01:14.240
-Yeah. Yeah.

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:16.342
It was a tough
first period for me.

00:01:16.342 --> 00:01:18.511
But, you know,
you have to stick to the game

00:01:18.511 --> 00:01:22.681
and do whatever you can
to help the guys be in the game

00:01:22.681 --> 00:01:24.650
and help them to win.

00:01:24.650 --> 00:01:27.854
-You're a tough --
-It doesn't matter what happens.

00:01:27.854 --> 00:01:32.224
You know, guys getting hit,
guys getting back, sacrifice --

00:01:32.224 --> 00:01:33.759
sacrifice their body.

00:01:33.759 --> 00:01:35.794
It's part of the playoffs.

00:01:35.794 --> 00:01:38.464
-Steven, as the captain,
what do --

00:01:38.464 --> 00:01:41.901
You're in game five.
And it's double OT.

00:01:41.901 --> 00:01:44.403
Here's my theory.
Maybe I'm wrong.

00:01:44.403 --> 00:01:47.707
Do you go like, "Hey, guys,
let's just get rid of this,

00:01:47.707 --> 00:01:50.242
give them the game tonight,
we'll get a good night's sleep,

00:01:50.242 --> 00:01:53.446
and then we're going to come out
and kill them on game six"?

00:01:53.446 --> 00:01:55.647
Is that a theory at all or no?

00:01:55.647 --> 00:01:58.250
-You got it, Jimmy.
You could do my job no problem.

00:01:58.250 --> 00:02:00.319
-Thank you, thank you.
That's all I wanted to hear.

00:02:00.319 --> 00:02:01.854
-That was it.

00:02:01.854 --> 00:02:04.523
I mean, the Cup was in
the building for game five.

00:02:04.523 --> 00:02:06.192
You can't not think about it.

00:02:06.192 --> 00:02:07.960
And then to lose
in double overtime,

00:02:07.960 --> 00:02:11.331
we just told the guys, like,
we played great, keep going.

00:02:11.331 --> 00:02:14.300
I think that was the best game
we've ever played, was game six.

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:18.037
-Yeah. I agree.
Victor, you won MVP.

00:02:18.037 --> 00:02:21.174
How does it feel
to be better than everybody?

00:02:21.174 --> 00:02:22.642
[ Laughter ]

00:02:22.642 --> 00:02:24.677
-Oh, I don't know about that.

00:02:24.677 --> 00:02:27.479
-No, I just wanted to get
a reaction from the guys.

00:02:27.479 --> 00:02:29.648
How does it feel
to be named MVP?

00:02:29.648 --> 00:02:31.184
It's got to feel good.

00:02:31.184 --> 00:02:33.720
-Yeah, that was unbelievable.
I did not expect it at all.

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:36.322
And, you know,
at the end of the day,

00:02:36.322 --> 00:02:39.258
the Cup you play for
is obviously this one.

00:02:39.258 --> 00:02:43.663
So, this could have gone to each
and every one on this team.

00:02:43.663 --> 00:02:48.001
But, you know, having my name
on this Cup means the world.

00:02:48.001 --> 00:02:50.402
-What is the first name
that you look at

00:02:50.402 --> 00:02:53.039
when you look
at the Stanley Cup?

00:02:53.039 --> 00:02:54.874
-I think, like,
Wayne Gretzky, for us,

00:02:54.874 --> 00:02:56.542
for my generation coming up.

00:02:56.542 --> 00:03:00.346
You see that name,
it's -- it's all over the Cup.

00:03:00.346 --> 00:03:02.781
So it's -- It was pretty funny.

00:03:02.781 --> 00:03:05.551
He actually FaceTimed
Patrick Maroon after the game,

00:03:05.551 --> 00:03:09.555
and The Great One was there.
-Wow.

00:03:09.555 --> 00:03:11.991
-Unbelievable
to have that moment.

00:03:11.991 --> 00:03:13.692
So that --
I thought that was pretty cool.

00:03:13.692 --> 00:03:16.095
-I have to say,
in times like this, you know,

00:03:16.095 --> 00:03:19.131
we're looking for
any good news at all.

00:03:19.131 --> 00:03:21.367
We need good news.
We need things to celebrate.

00:03:21.367 --> 00:03:23.335
And you guys gave us
something to celebrate,

00:03:23.335 --> 00:03:24.837
and you gave us some good news.

00:03:24.837 --> 00:03:26.672
So thank you so much for that
as a fan.

00:03:26.672 --> 00:03:29.308
And congrats again
on winning the Stanley Cup.

00:03:29.308 --> 00:03:31.310
-Thanks, Jimmy!
-Steven Stamkos,

00:03:31.310 --> 00:03:33.412
Nikita Kucherov,
and Victor Hedman.

00:03:33.412 --> 00:03:35.415
Thank you so much
for being here.

